Skipped by `colcon build`, on purpose.

This package declares build_type ament_python in package.xml but deliberately
has no setup.py of its own: pip installation for the whole repo is consolidated
in the root setup.py, so that there is exactly one way to install everything
(see that file's docstring, and ../../README.md). colcon would try to build it
and fail on the missing setup.py, taking neo_msgs and neo_bringup down with it.

So the two install paths are split, and both work:

  pip install -e ".[dev]"   -> this package and the other three
  colcon build              -> neo_msgs and neo_bringup

That is enough to run the ROS nodes: rclpy finds neo_msgs from the sourced
colcon overlay, and finds this package because pip put it on the Python path.
What it does NOT provide is `ros2 run` / `ros2 launch` discovery of this
package's executables, which need an ament index entry.

Remove this file, and add a per-package setup.py, in the phase that first needs
`ros2 run` for this package -- not before. Until then the root setup.py's
console_scripts are the entry points.
